why_this_one:
It is the whole of the client's Twister, in the *release* arm of MoveCharacter - the arm Flame is made in, when c->AttackTime reaches g_iLimitAttackTime - at ZzzCharacter.cpp:4495:

    case AT_SKILL_STORM:
        CreateEffect(MODEL_STORM, o->Position, o->Angle, Light, 0, o, o->PKKey, FindHotKey(AT_SKILL_STORM));
        PlayBuffer(SOUND_STORM);
        break;

One model and one wave. Everything else - the smoke at its foot, the two thin bolts coming down into it, the stones it kicks up, the dark it puts on the ground - is Move_MODEL_STORM's sub-type 0 arm, run every frame of its life.

*Where it starts and which way it goes.* At the caster's own position and angle, not at the tile he aimed at: MU's client sends Twister's request with `c->PositionX, c->PositionY` and his facing (ClassAttack.cpp:1358), where Flame's sends the target tile. The create arm gives it `Direction = (0, -10, 0)` and the shared tail of MoveEffect walks it with `MoveParticle(o, true)` - that direction rotated by the effect's own angle - so the storm crosses ten units a frame straight out along the way he was facing, and its own `o->Position[2] = RequestTerrainHeight(...)` every frame keeps it on the ground as it goes.
